Summary of that file (verified 2026-10-25, sources cited there): two components
(jump3r and jaudiotagger) are LGPL, and their licence texts ship inside this
repository under docs/licenses/. Poolakey, which an earlier revision of this
file flagged as GPL-3.0, is Apache-2.0 according to its own repository — there
is no GPL component in the build. Adivery is proprietary and used under its own
service terms (bazaar flavour only).

If you would prefer an open-source licence instead (MIT/Apache-2.0 are the usual
choices for an app like this), replace this file — but read the LGPL/GPL notes
above first, because they constrain what you may choose.
